&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Net Operating Loss Carryforwards&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;We have federal and state net operating loss carryforwards for which deferred tax assets of approximately $86.9 million have been recorded as of December 31, 2025. The most significant of these net operating loss carryforwards will expire beginning in 2036. We believe that we will be able to generate sufficient taxable income in the future to utilize all of our net operating loss carryforwards. Therefore, no valuation allowance has been recorded for the deferred tax assets associated with these net operating loss carryforwards as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
