&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;KMI and substantially all of its wholly owned domestic subsidiaries, including us, are a party to a cross guarantee agreement whereby each party to the agreement unconditionally guarantees, jointly and severally, the payment of specified indebtedness of each other party to the agreement.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;6. Rate and Regulatory Matters&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Lake Charles Expansion Project (CP14-511-000)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On June 30, 2014, we filed an application with the FERC seeking authorization to construct (i) new low and high pressure natural gas header pipelines adjacent to our existing easement in Acadia Parish, Louisiana, (ii) a new 64,000 horsepower compressor station in Evangeline Parish, Louisiana, (iii) modifications to five existing meter stations in Acadia and Evangeline Parishes, Louisiana to make them bi-directional and (iv) a new meter station in Calcasieu Parish, Louisiana to deliver gas to Magnolia LNG, LLC (Magnolia) at its proposed liquefaction and export facility (Magnolia LNG terminal). The proposed construction and system modifications will provide 1.4 billion cubic feet per day of firm north-to-south transportation capacity to deliver natural gas to the proposed terminal (CP14-347-000). The total filed cost of the project is $201.9 million. Our application, as well as the application for construction of the Magnolia LNG terminal, was approved by the FERC on April 15, 2016. We accepted the certificate on May 12, 2016. On September 11, 2020, we and Magnolia filed a joint request at the FERC for an extension of time to place these facilities in service. On October 7, 2020, the FERC issued an order granting an extension of time until April 15, 2026 to complete construction of the Magnolia LNG terminal and Lake Charles Expansion Project and make them available for service.&amp;#160; The project shipper has not made a final investment decision on the project.&amp;#160; We are evaluating our options regarding vacating the certificate authorization granted in this docket.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Texas Access Project (TAP) (CP 26-136) &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On March 6, 2026, we filed an application with the FERC seeking authorization to construct an approximately 3 mile extension of our interstate natural gas pipeline system and certain related facilities located in Jefferson County, Texas and Cameron Parish, Louisiana, and a new interconnection with Louisiana LNG Gas Management LLC's&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;new LNG terminal on our existing mainline in Calcasieu&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Parish, Louisiana.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The project is designed to provide shippers with firm transportation from Texas to new and existing markets in South Louisiana. This proposed $112 million project will provide 1.3 Bcf/d of firm transportation capacity. We have requested issuance of a certificate order authorizing the project by February 2027.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The anticipated in-service date is second quarter of 2028.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Regulatory Assets and Liabilities&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, the regulatory assets are subject to recovery in our rates, over a period of approximately one year to 19 years. Below are the details of our regulatory assets and liabilities (in millions):&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
